<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md, D6.1) - BUYER ACTIVITY TIMELINE,
        SCHEMA HALF.

        🔴 THIS FIELD IS BOTH ANALYST-ENTERED AND MACHINE-DEFAULTED - NOT ONE OR THE OTHER.
        SCHEMA ONLY SHIPS IN THIS CHANGE; THE DEFAULT-STAMPING IS A LATER DEVELOPER STEP.
        A pure default cannot express "materials went to buyer A on Tuesday and buyer B on
        Friday", which is the entire point of tracking this per-buyer (per-NDA) rather than once
        on the parent Disposition. A pure manual field would be blank on most rows and the
        timeline's middle hop would disappear. The intended shape, to be built by the developer
        agent in DispositionStageEntryService alongside openBuyerNdas / stampListingDates /
        openBrokerListings: on entry to the Release Materials stage, stamp this field on every
        buyer-role NDA where it is still null - IDEMPOTENT AND BLANK-ONLY, never overwriting an
        analyst's own entry, the same shape as NDA_Signed_Status_Sync's Date_Signed_Is_Blank gate
        and openBuyerNdas's idempotency guard. The analyst can always override afterward for the
        exceptions (a buyer who received materials on a different day).

        NDA__c IS A DUAL-MODULE OBJECT (serves Acquisitions and Dispositions). This field is
        inert on the acquisition side and is deliberately NOT added to any acquisition-specific
        permission set or layout in this change.

        🔴 FLS: A Metadata API deployed custom field arrives with NO field permissions for any
        profile, System Administrator included. Read and edit are granted in
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit, read only in DPEG_Disposition_View, in the same change. Neither
        acquisition permission set nor DPEG_Admin_Access is touched.
    -->
    <fullName>Materials_Released_Date__c</fullName>
    <description>Date the deal package/materials were released to the buyer named on this NDA. Analyst-entered, and later also default-stamped (blank-only, idempotent) on entry to the Release Materials stage by a developer-owned step - see in-file comment. Inert on acquisition NDAs.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>When materials went out to this buyer. Usually set automatically when the disposition enters Release Materials; edit it if this buyer's materials went out on a different day.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Materials Released Date</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Date</type>
</CustomField>
